# Choosing a backend and a model

The neighbour. Its table offers exactly the values this plugin answers to, and a
reader that returned nothing whatever it was shown would pass both refusal legs
without it.

## What you set the backend to

| Setting value | What it transcribes with | What the operator supplies |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `None` | Nothing. | Nothing. |
| `Local` | A whisper.cpp compatible command line tool. | The tool, and a model file. |
| `Remote` | An HTTP endpoint. | A base URL, and a key if the endpoint wants one. |

## What the tree holds today

No run of this plugin has ever produced a subtitle.
